//
// AN OPERATOR LIVES WITH ITS TYPE (`@FR-Op-Home`).  An operator on a built-in type, or on a type another
// source declares, is refused where it is written.  Each function is one refusal with its
// expectation.
//
// ── an-operator-on-a-built-in-type-is-refused ──
//
// AN OPERATOR ON A BUILT-IN TYPE IS REFUSED (`@FR-Op-Home`: "the `self` type of an `operator`
// definition is declared in the same source as the definition; on a built-in type it is
// refused"): `operator times(self: boolean, …)` would give `*` a meaning on `boolean` that no
// program declared, so it is refused at the definition.  One refusal per file.
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; the refusal fired as expected on 18594597b,
//   interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile (the expected diagnostic).
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the built-in type.
// HOLDS: the same definition on a struct of this file compiles (Op-Name's cell).
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `operator times` defines `*` for a type of its own package, and `boolean` is not one
//
// ── an-operator-on-another-sources-type-is-refused ──
//
// AN OPERATOR ON ANOTHER SOURCE'S TYPE IS REFUSED (`@FR-Op-Home`): `OhPt` is declared in the
// fixture library `op_home_fixture_lib.loft` beside this file, so only that source may define an
// operator on it — a consumer's `operator minus(self: OhPt, …)` would give `-` a meaning the
// type's author never wrote, and two consumers could give it two.  Refused at the definition,
// pointing at an ordinary method.  One refusal per file.
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; the refusal fired as expected on 18594597b,
//   interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile (the expected diagnostic).
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the foreign type.
// HOLDS: the library's own `operator plus` on `OhPt` works (the fixture cell).
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `operator minus` on `OhPt` can only be defined where `OhPt` is declared

use op_home_fixture_lib::*;

operator times(self: boolean, o: integer) -> integer { if self { o } else { 0 } }



operator minus(self: OhPt, o: OhPt) -> OhPt { OhPt { x: self.x - o.x } }

fn test_an_operator_on_another_sources_type_is_refused() {
  a = OhPt { x: 1 };
  println("{a.minus(a).x}");
}
